# Base URL of the backend API
VITE_API_URL="http://localhost:4000/api/v1"

# Basemap tiles for the network map.
#
# NCA chose an open-source tile server (3 September 2026). OpenStreetMap's own tiles are set below
# so the map works out of the box.
#
# Worth being explicit about the trade, because it is a real one: every tile request tells the
# server which part of the map is being looked at, and NCA's operators look at their own masts.
# That is not the mast coordinates themselves — those never leave the portal — but it is a
# reasonable inference about where the Authority is working. OSM's public tiles also carry a usage
# policy that a busy internal tool can exceed.
#
# Both are answered the same way, and it is worth doing before this carries real traffic: run a
# tile server inside NCA's own network and point this at it. Nothing else changes.
VITE_MAP_TILE_URL="https://tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png"
VITE_MAP_TILE_ATTRIBUTION="© OpenStreetMap contributors"
